{
  "summary": "Reuses a single FuzzedWallet instance across iterations in the wallet fuzz harnesses instead of rebuilding it per input. A new test-only method CWallet::ClearInMemoryTxStateForTest resets transaction and coin-spend maps in memory without reimporting keys or touching descriptor state. FuzzedWallet now precomputes a destination pool, clears wallet transaction state per run, and periodically rebuilds the wallet after every 1000 iterations.",
  "problem": "Constructing FuzzedWallet for every fuzz iteration imports eight descriptors and incurs BIP32 derivations and multiple database transactions before reaching the target code, severely limiting fuzz execution throughput.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author reports a ~6x speedup on an Ubuntu machine without sanitizers (PR description)."
