  "changed_since_previous": "Added a periodic rebuild every 1000 iterations to bound wallet state growth and an RAII drift check asserting bounded descriptor range movement during test execution.",
  "card": "This pull request optimizes wallet fuzzing by caching a single FuzzedWallet across inputs rather than reconstructing it every iteration. It adds a test-only CWallet::ClearInMemoryTxStateForTest method to wipe in-memory transaction and spend maps, while FuzzedWallet pools precomputed destinations and rebuilds every 1000 iterations. Rebuilding the wallet per input was paying descriptor imports and BIP32 derivation costs on every test run. The author benchmarks a roughly 6x speedup without sanitizers.",
